<Layout title="Concept Privacy Notice" description="How this independent static redesign concept handles your information."><section class="page-heading section"><p class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT CONCEPT</p><h1>A clear view<br/>of <em>your privacy.</em></h1></section><article class="legal section"><p>Updated October 13, 2026. This notice applies to this independent website concept, which is not the official Silicon Valley General Builder Contractor website.</p><h2>Contact form</h2><p>The form validates your entries in your browser and prepares an email draft. There is no server submission, lead database, or automatic email delivery. Opening your email app transfers the prepared information to that app; sending is your choice.</p><h2>Browser storage</h2><p>The site uses session storage only to remember whether the brief opening animation has played. It adds no advertising cookies or analytics.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Images, fonts, scripts, and the company logo are served locally. Telephone and email links open the relevant application on your device. If deployed, the hosting provider may process technical access logs under its own policies.</p><h2>Company information</h2><p>Company facts and attributed review excerpts are sourced from the public company website. This concept is not endorsed by the company. Published license information is not a live license-status check.</p><h2>Production launch</h2><p>A production website would need an approved privacy policy, hosting disclosures, an agreed retention policy, and a properly secured contact integration before collecting requests.</p></article></Layout>
